DATA NOTICE: mnist

Data files tracked by DVC in this directory (fetch with `dvc pull`):
  data.zip -> data/{train,t10k}-{images.idx3,labels.idx1}-ubyte

What:
  The MNIST database of handwritten digits: 60,000 training and 10,000
  test images (28x28) with labels, in IDX format.

Attribution:
  The MNIST database, Yann LeCun, Corinna Cortes and Christopher J.C.
  Burges, http://yann.lecun.com/exdb/mnist/. MNIST is a derivative
  work of the NIST Special Databases 1 and 3.

Changes:
  None. The four files are byte-identical to the standard MNIST files
  (checked 2026-11-19 against the PyTorch mirror
  https://ossci-datasets.s3.amazonaws.com/mnist/, after gunzip); only
  the file names use '.' instead of '-' before "idx".

